00053Dr 1               
00053Dr 1               ; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
00053Dr 1               ; Pixels.  The screen is kept in RAM as block graphics characters: want[]
00053Dr 1               ; is what it should show, shown[] what the terminal shows (80 x 24 each).
00053Dr 1               ; setpix / clrpix change want[] and note the character in a list; flush_px
00053Dr 1               ; sends the characters that differ, one byte each (plus cursor moves), which
00053Dr 1               ; is much less than 3 bytes per pixel when creatures move.
00053Dr 1               ; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
00053Dr 1               
00053Dr 1               ; set / reset the pixel at X, Y.  Preserves X and Y.
00053Dr 1  20 rr rr     setpix: jsr     px_cell
000540r 1  8D rr rr             sta     pmask
000543r 1  20 rr rr             jsr     want_rd
000546r 1  8D rr rr             sta     pold
